WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Last night
I went out to dinner.

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:02.535 line:92%
You were also at the restaurant.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was lovely
to see you beforehand.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:04.938 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-It was good to see you.

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:06.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
Except, you know,
I was wearing a lovely outfit.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:10.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had a blue blazer,
a white shirt and khaki pants,

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:13.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so were the waiters --
exactly the same.

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:13.613 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:14.814 line:92%
-So when I went to the toilet,

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:15.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
someone asked me
for their oysters.

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:18.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Dude."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:21.654
-I was -- 'cause when I saw you,
you looked great in clothes.

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:24.557
I saw your outfit, I go, "Man,
Idris has got it figured out."

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:26.159 size:88% position:44%
And then I walked in the
restaurant and realized,

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:27.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, Idris has a problem."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.231
Yeah. Idris is about to find out
he has a problem.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.599 line:92%
You were very nice, as well.

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:34.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
You asked about my mother.
-Hillary.

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:36.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, my mom Hillary.
-How is she?

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:37.037 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-She's great.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:39.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
You met her a few years ago
at a party in L.A.

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:40.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
-She was a huge fan of yours.

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:42.909
You were very kind to her.
-She told you about that?

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She did tell me about that,
yeah.

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:45.478 size:78% position:39% line:92%
She told my dad, too.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
She pretty much brings you up
to my dad every day.

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:48.882 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:49.616 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
His name is Larry.

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:51.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
Since she met you,
she calls him "Not Idris."

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:52.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:56.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh! Larry, Larry.
That's not nice. Sorry, Larry.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:58.158 size:78% position:39%
-But here, I want you
to know something,

00:00:58.158 --> 00:00:59.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
because she's a huge fan of
yours.

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:02.062
But there's an opening right now
for you, because the top --

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:02.695 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You're not the top.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:05.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
The top is always, for my mom,
Daniel Day-Lewis.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Who?
-Daniel Day-Lewis.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:08.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm just joking.
-Wonderful actor.

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:08.768 line:92%
-Yeah, I know, very good.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:10.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You should definitely look at
his work.

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:13.406
But you know, now he's saying
he might get out of the game.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:14.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes! No!
-Exactly.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:15.742 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-But I'm just saying,

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you keep up
your high quality of work,

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like you could hit
that new pinnacle for my mom.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:20.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:24.684 size:84% position:42%
-Again? Just joking.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:25.618 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
No, no, no.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:30.156 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:31.224 line:92%
No, no, no. This is awkward.

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:34.861
-It's great. No, like six hours
from now, when this airs,

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:37.630 size:78% position:39%
the roof of our home,
my childhood home,

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:40.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
is gonna blow off.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:42.602 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Larry's like, "Who?"

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.170 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-"Why?!"

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.039 line:92%
Congratulations on this film.

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:49.175
This is a series of eight books,
the "Dark Tower" books.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:49.843 size:81% position:41% line:92%
This is the first one.

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:53.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you a fan of this sort of
fantasy/horror genre?

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:54.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what?
I'm a fan of Stephen King.

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:58.184
I think he's an incredible
author. Right? He's great.

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:00.153 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:01.254 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He's a little dark.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:04.224
-Yeah, he's a little dark.
This one's particularly dark.

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:07.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But "The Shining" --
I was a fan of "The Shining."

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:07.861 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And also Jack Nicholson.

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:10.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know, I wanted to be
in a blockbuster.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:12.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wanted to play a big hero
in a film.

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:16.936
And who better than Stephen King
to be the author of that?

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:17.604 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-And it was interesting.

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:20.340
I read an article where
Ron Howard, as a producer, said

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.207 line:92%
that when they were casting it,

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:23.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
the character -- Stephen King
wrote the character

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:25.378
to be sort of the biggest badass
in the world.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:26.446 line:92%
And when they started saying,

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:27.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Who currently
is the biggest badass?"

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:30.283
They said you came up
right away. That's high praise.

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:31.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:33.186 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:34.487 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you. Thanks.

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:39.058
But, no, they cast me because
Stephen King actually wanted

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:40.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
Clint Eastwood.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:42.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And said, "Who looks like
Clint Eastwood?"

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:44.063 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:47.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Blatantly me, so that's how
that worked out.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:47.567 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:49.035
That worked out great,
and I should point out --

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:51.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
it wasn't in the clip,
but the villain in this film,

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:53.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
the wonderful
Matthew McConaughey.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-I feel like that's a good --

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:57.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys are
a good yin and yang.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.945
-Matthew's great. And he's
really good in the film.

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:03.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's very different.
He's very stoic, evil guy.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:03.850 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:06.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In real life.
Just joking, Matt.

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:09.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
But no, in the film,
he's really good. He's great.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:09.989 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's great.

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:12.759
Was this one of those action
films where you have to do

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:14.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of training,
and a lot of figuring out

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:14.928 size:78% position:39% line:92%
how to play the part?

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:17.964
-Yeah, 'cause we wanted --
The film is quite grounded.

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:20.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Dark Tower"
is quite grounded.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:21.334 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:24.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, it looked like a normal,
everyday thing, yeah.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:27.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But no, the director,
Nik Arcel, wanted us to --

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.211
at least the gunslinging,
all the shooting and stuff.

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:33.580 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Six-shooting is a sport.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
Reloading and shooting
on target,

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:36.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that's where
I started my training.

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:38.585
And we wanted to make that look
as real as possible.

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:40.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Great.
Did you get to be okay at it?

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm great at it.
-Oh, okay.

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:44.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
You didn't have to jump all
the way to great.

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:45.925 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:49.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, but -- I had an amazing
time making that film.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:50.463 line:92%
We shot it in South Africa,

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
which has some of the most
beautiful landscapes

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the world,
in the eastern cape.

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:56.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we shot in L.A.
as well.

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:59.305
-And this is very exciting --
We were talking last night.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:00.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
You directed your first film?
-Yeah.

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:04.344
-And so this is based on a book
called "Yardie" from the '80s?

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:05.278 line:92%
Is that when it was written?

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:06.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, so it's a novel
from the '80s

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:09.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
which follows a young Jamaican
boy that ends up in London

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:14.454
and becomes a gangster,
and he's not really a gangster.

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:15.255 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And I chose that film

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:18.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
because England has
a big Jamaican community.

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:21.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm West African, but
the Jamaican community sort of

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:24.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the overriding influential
black community.

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:26.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I felt very connected
to the story,

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:29.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I wanted to see it happen,
and I loved it.

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:31.371
It was probably the best
experience as a filmmaker,

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:34.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
as an actor, to direct a film
because you're talking to

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:38.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
every single department about
so many different levels,

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:39.412 line:92%
It was wicked. It was great.

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:41.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
-As a director, did you then
look back and say,

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:45.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, Idris the actor had been
unfair to directors"?

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, completely.
-Really? Yeah.

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:48.221 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No, seriously.

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:51.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the worst people
I hated on my set was actors.

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:52.692 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:53.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Divas.
-Divas.

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:56.329
-What? Get here on time.
What, you don't know your lines?

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:58.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
Get out of here!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:59.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, but I had a great time
being able

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:03.369
to speak the language of acting
but not be on camera.

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:04.003 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-That's really exciting.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now, we've also talked
about this.

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:06.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're also a deejay.
-Yep.

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:08.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because you have to be good
at everything

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:10.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
and make the rest of us
feel bad.

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:12.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, you're a six-shooter
and a deejay

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:16.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my mom's favorite person.
No, it's great.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:18.384 line:92%
-Kind of like your stepdad.

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:20.987 line:92%
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:23.589
-I'm sorry, Dad.
I shouldn't have brought it up.

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:26.459 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You set that up.

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:28.795
-That would be awesome, though.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:30.997
I would love, just like --
I mean, it wouldn't be a lot.

00:05:30.997 --> 00:05:34.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just like one weekend a month?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:36.069 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:38.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you've done some
soundtracks of films before?

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:41.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I did --
so, for "Luther," my TV show,

00:05:41.741 --> 00:05:43.109 line:92%
I made a soundtrack for that.

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:47.113
And basically what I do is take
the themes of the show

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:51.150 size:88% position:44%
and work with musicians
and make original songs.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.386 size:84% position:42%
I did one for "Luther,"
did one for "Mandela,"

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:55.722 size:84% position:42%
and I'm going to do one
for "Yardie" as well.

